{
  "fixture": "wrap-and-split",
  "version": 1,
  "format": {
    "row_width": "The measured row TRACK width in px: the content column plus the 6px box bleed on each side.",
    "rects": "[left, top, width, height] in track coordinates. Compare with a tolerance of 0.01.",
    "boundaries": "The centre of each column gap in track coordinates; only for unwrapped rows (cols == count).",
    "rows": "A row is [rowId, [[widgetId, width], ...], height?]. The height defaults to 360, a widget's view_id is view-<widgetId> and its database_id is db. A duplicate keeps the view_id and database_id of its source.",
    "ids": "\"*\" in an expected row matches a generated id.",
    "placement": "{\"type\": \"existing_row\", \"row_id\": \"r1\", \"index\": 0} or {\"type\": \"new_row\", \"row_index\": 1}; an absent index means the end.",
    "op": "add {widget, placement}, remove {widget}, move {widget, placement}, duplicate {widget}, set_height {row, height}.",
    "unchanged": "true: the result deep-equals the input rows (ids, heights, widths). For a move, classify gives noop, or the feedback value when one is given.",
    "expect": "The rows after the operation, compared by row id, height, widget ids and widths.",
    "row_controls": "getDashboardRowControls(rows, rowId) for each listed row id: move_up, move_down and add_to_row (enabled, disabled or hidden); an unknown row id gives false, false, hidden. add_to_new_row is getDashboardAddToNewRowState(rows): enabled or disabled.",
    "drop": "Dragging widget `source` onto `target`: {\"type\": \"widget\", \"widget_id\": \"b\", \"edge\": \"left\" | \"right\"} or {\"type\": \"row_gap\", \"row_index\": 1} (0 = above the first row, rows.length = below the last). feedback is getDashboardDropFeedback (allowed, blocked or noop). placement is resolveDashboardDropPlacement: the positional placement, null only for an unknown source or target or a drop on the source itself; a drop applies it only when feedback is allowed. indicator is getDashboardDropIndicator, null unless allowed: {\"type\": \"column\", \"row_id\": \"r1\", \"boundary\": 2} (the insert position 0..n in the row before the source leaves it) or {\"type\": \"row_gap\", \"row_index\": 1}. expect (allowed drops only) is moveDashboardWidget(rows, source, placement).",
    "menu": "The widget menu of `widget`. move_targets is getWidgetMoveTargets: left, right, row_above and row_below placements, or null. entries is buildWidgetMenuEntries({editing, canDuplicate: the dashboard has a free widget slot, moveTargets}) in display order, each {id, group, disabled, disabled_reason?, children?}; a separator goes between two groups."
  },
